Z||000002||artherd||09-28-2001||04:01 AM||||<BR>The cop was probally stoping you more for 'not looking out for cops well enough" heh.<P>Sounds like a cool guy, and so long as we're not doing it in a residential neighborhood at 1am, and are in controle of the vehicle, and there's no one in sight, most cops won't bother you.<P>PS: that is how to properly drive a fiero!!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTMike:<BR><B><BR>he comes back<BR>officer: well i have taken a linking to you because i to like to lightem up every once in a while.  just try not to do it infront of a cop next time. <P>that made my day... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Awesome!!  The local police here participate in wendsday night drag races at Sears Point (actually, I belive the local LE depts got together and went and sponsored it and everything)  You get to drag race actual cops in cop cars too, it's great!!<P>Brilliant idea on several counts.<BR>(gets the itch for draging off the streets and onto a timed 1/4mile, and turns cops from the enemy into REALLY COOL PEOPLE.)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
